course: dictionary
lesson: 7501
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word pot can mean a cooking container, a flowerpot, a jar of food, or even a lot of money. «Pot and pan handles should be turned inward so nobody can knock or grab them.» Here pots and pans are for cooking, so pot means a deep round container for cooking.
explain: Now try a gardening sentence. «Mum set the seedlings in a pot on the windowsill.» A seedling is a young plant, and a windowsill is a place for plants, so this pot is a flowerpot. Always ask: which meaning fits these clues? Then test your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Pot can also be a verb. To pot a plant is to put it into a pot, so the word works as an action as well as a thing. In a maths question, pots are containers you count. Pots needed = plants ÷ plants per pot, rounded up, because a half-full pot still needs a pot.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A pot is a deep round container for cooking, like a saucepan.
fact: A pot can be a flowerpot, a teapot, or a pot of jam.
fact: To pot a plant means to put it in a pot.
fact: «Pots of money» means a lot of money, and «a watched pot never boils» means time feels slower when you stare and wait.
exercise: «Pot and pan handles should be turned inward so nobody can knock or grab them.» In this sentence, pot most likely means | a flowerpot | a pot of money | *a cooking container | a sort of hat
exercise: A gardener has 12 seedlings and each pot holds 3 seedlings. How many pots are needed? | 36 | *4 | 3 | 9
exercise: Nadia says «A watched pot never boils» is about water. What does the saying really mean? | Watching is bad for your eyes | *Time feels slower when you stare and wait | Water boils faster when you watch it | Pots must never be left on the stove
test:  To pot a plant means | to cut off its dead leaves | to dig it up from the garden | *to put it in a pot | to water it every day
test: A gardener has 20 plants and each pot holds 6 plants. How many pots are needed, rounded up? | 5 | 20 | *4 | 3
exam: In «a pot of jam», pot means | *a container for food | a lot of money | to put something in a pot | a plant growing in soil
